<clickhouse>
    <!--
    Override the image's default docker_related_config.xml, which declares both
    `<listen_host>::</listen_host>` (IPv6 wildcard) and `0.0.0.0`.

    On Docker environments where IPv6 is unavailable, binding `[::]` fails with
    "DNS error: EAI: Address family for hostname not supported". Because the
    image also sets `<listen_try>1</listen_try>`, the server keeps running
    instead of crashing — and on clickhouse-server 26.x the failed IPv6 bind
    leaves 8123/9000 unbound entirely.

    The failure is silent from the outside: the compose healthcheck uses
    clickhouse-client (local connection, not the TCP listeners), so the
    container still reports healthy while every HTTP client times out. That
    surfaces in the app as "Prompts Are Unavailable" even though the data is
    intact.

    Pinning a single IPv4 wildcard keeps the HTTP (8123) and native (9000)
    listeners deterministic regardless of host IPv6 support.
    -->
    <listen_host replace="replace">0.0.0.0</listen_host>
</clickhouse>
